OL,3,APioneering fossil hunter recognised
OL,4,Awith blue plaque
OL,5,
OL,6,FA pioneering fossil hunter who was one
OL,7,Fof the first women to be employed by
OL,8,Fthe National History Museum has been
OL,9,Frecognised with a national blue plaque.
OL,11,FDorothea Bate, who died in 1951 aged
OL,12,F72, "transformed our understanding of
OL,13,Fprehistoric animals and ancient
OL,14,Fenvironments" through her research,
OL,15,FHistoric England said.
OL,23,APub: 07-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
