OL,3,APioneering fossil hunter recognised
OL,4,Awith blue plaque
OL,5,
OL,6,FShe has been recognised with a plaque
OL,7,Fat the National History Museum in
OL,8,FTring, Hertfordshire, which notes in
OL,9,Fits inscription that the
OL,10,Fpalaeontologist was the
OL,11,F"Officer-in-Charge of this museum from
OL,12,F1948".
OL,14,FBate was born in Carmarthen, Wales, in
OL,15,F1878 and developed a fascination with
OL,16,Fthe natural world from an early age.
